Version: 2010_v1.0.0
............................................................................................................................
This is the code which was used for the 2010a 0.323E+20 POT muon-disappearance analysis.
Details may be found in T2K-TN-36 (v4).

Version: 2010_v2.0.0 
............................................................................................................................
This is the code which was used for the 2010b 1.431E+20 POT muon-disappearance analysis.
Details may be found in T2K-TN-64 (v3).

The following changes were installed (wrt 2010_v1.0.0) :
> Upgraded SK flux (10d_v2 --> 10d_v3). The official 10d_v3 flux was obtained from: 
  http://www.t2k.org/beam/NuFlux/FluxRelease/10d/10dtunev3
> Upgraded Nsk/Nnd error calculation code (v2.2 -> v3.1). The updated error calculation code was downloaded from: 
  http://www.t2k.org/beam/NuFlux/FluxRelease/10d/nsknnderrv3
> Upgraded flux shape error (v2.2 -> v3.1). The updated flux fractional covariance matrix was downloaded from: 
  http://www.t2k.org/beam/NuFlux/FluxRelease/10d/shapeerrorv31
> Used the updated ND280 event histograms (updated with 10d_v3 flux). The histograms were downloaded from: 
  http://www.t2k.org/asg/oagroup/nd280-offaxis/
> Used revised SuperK ring-counting (RC) efficiency errors computed by M.Otani and J.Kameda.
  numu CCQE RC eff. err.:   
    7.6% --> 1.7% (Ereco<0.4GeV), 3.5% (0.4GeV<Ereco<1.1GeV), 9.3% (Ereco>1.1GeV)
                             /   (1.7%)^2    0.59 * 1.7% * 3.5%    0.33 * 1.7% * 9.3% \
       + covariance matrix = |                   (3.5%)^2          0.61 * 3.5% * 9.3% |
                             \                                         (9.3%)^2       /
  numu CCnonQE  RC eff. err.:  
    25.4% --> 19.9%
  numu/nutau NC RC eff. err.:  
    57.0% --> 48.2%
  The updated RC efficiency error brings the total FC 1-ring mu-like efficiency err 
  (fiducial + reduction + OD cut + RC + PID + momentum cut + decay e cut) is
  numu CCQE eff. err.:   
    7.8% -->   1.7% + RC shape error given above.
  numu CCnonQE eff. err.:  
    25.5% -->  20.0%
  numu/nutau NC eff. err.: 
    115.1% --> 111.0%
  Details are given in: T2K-TN-65
> Used revised SuperK energy scale error (1% --> 2.3%) computed by Obayashi.
  Details are given in: ?
> Added analysis configuration files for Run1-only, Run2-only and Run1+Run2 analysis, both for NEUT and GENIE. 
  The Run1+Run2 flux is a POT-weighted 10d_v3 flux (taking into account Run1 and Run2 flux differences).

In addition, the code structure was modified significantly to allow for future analysis improvements.

2010_v2.1.0
............................................................................................................................

Similar to 2010_v2.0.0 but with the following change requested during the analysis review:

> The nd280 efficiency error was increased from +/-5% to +5.6% -5.2% to match the one used in the nue analysis.
> The statistical error of the ND280 CC inclusive measurement (~2.7%) was also propagated to SK.


2010_v3.0.0
............................................................................................................................

This code was used for the 2010b 1.431E+20 POT 3-flavour muon-neutrino disappearance analysis (details in T2K-TN-88)
and for the 2010b 1.431E+20 POT joint 3-flavour analysis (details in T2K-TN-131)

Similar to 2010_v2.1.0 but with the following additions: 

> Added option to fit for systematics (any/all of the ~30-40 systematic parameters considered in 2010 analysis).
> Added code to calculate oscillation probabilities in vacuum and matter in a 3-flavour framework.
> Modified numu disappearance analysis to work in 3-flavour framework.
  Capability to perform analysis in 2-flavour framework was retained for backward-compatibility.
  In the 3-flavour disappearance fit, oscillation parameters Dm^2_{12}, sin^2(2theta_{12}), sin^2(2theta_{13}) 
  and delta_{cp} can either a) be considered on equal footing as |Dm^2_{23}|, sin^2(2theta_{23}), b) fixed or
  c) treated as nuisance parameters and be marginalised. The latter option is used in our analysis (marginalization).
> Extended code so that it can also predict SK 1Re distributions and perform a 3-flavour nue appearance analysis.
> Extected code so it can perform a global numu disappearance + nue appearance analysis.
> For the oscillation analyses, add capability to fit for either sin^2(2*theta_ij) or sin^2(theta_ij) 
  depending on configuration options. Fitting for sin^2(theta_ij) is preferred for the global 3-flavour analysis.
> Added event templates from the `nue signal' MC (nue interactions generated with the numu flux). 
  Needed for the 3-flavour numu disappearance analysis and for the nue appearance analysis.
  The normalization factor for the sample used for the newly added `nue signal' templates is:
    nue(signal) / GENIE  :  1376.9700 events / 1E+21 POT / 22.5 kt fiducial mass
    nue(signal) / NEUT   :  ????.???? events / 1E+21 POT / 22.5 kt fiducial mass
> Minor update to the GENIE MC normalization, using flux histograms which were not affected by the `ignored decay modes'
  bug. The normalization factors were updated as follows:
    numu      : 1325.4200 --> 1323.6500 events / 1E+21 POT / 22.5 kt fiducial mass
    numubar   :   65.1023 -->   66.1802 events / 1E+21 POT / 22.5 kt fiducial mass
    nue(beam) :   25.9600 -->   26.1256 events / 1E+21 POT / 22.5 kt fiducial mass
> Many structural changes to allow the 3-flavour numu analysis and the global nue+numu 3-flavour analysis
> Committed a various macros used to prepare plots for T2K-TN-64 which previously weren't under version control


2012_v0.9.0
............................................................................................................................

A *major* re-write of the analysis to use the official 2012 inputs.
Contains numerous technical and physics improvements wrt to the 2010_* series of branches.
Details, too numerous to mention here, may be found in T2K-TN-141.
This is the first freeze of the fully validated 2012 code: This branch contains experimental and 
deprecated features that will be removed from a near-future "streamlined" revision.

2012_v1.0.0
............................................................................................................................

As 2012_v0.9.0 but drastically cleaned-up.
This is the code used for the official analysis.
Experimental FSI and BANFF systematic binnings, systematics not used in the analysis were removed. 
Deprecated data files, macros and scripts were removed. 
Code experimenting with the use of principal components analysis in the study of the effect of systematics 
in the oscillation fit was deleted.
The main Minuit and the experimental Minuit2 fit implementations were "unified" 
so that one can switch between the two transparently.

